@title Cabinet: a duct has end handles, a length with its bar and offcut, and trim buttons
@area Cabinet
@sizes 1366x768 1920x1080
# Rails and ducts window (palette: rails): add a duct, it is selected and the card under the list names its length
# and the bar it is cut from; Cut to length offers the stock lengths; a cut is one undo step. Pictures: window with
# the card, the cut menu, after a cut to 1000 mm, after undo. Dragging the end handles is covered by unit tests.
open qa/fixtures/cabinet-lesson.novo
wait 20
click_text Cabinet #1
wait 30
key ctrl+k
wait 3
text rails and ducts
wait 4
key Enter
wait 10
click_text "Add duct"
wait 10
expect "Cut from one 2000 mm bar"
expect "Trim at point"
shot card
click_text "Cut to length"
wait 5
expect "1000 mm"
shot cut-menu
click_text "1000 mm  (half a bar)"
wait 10
expect "Length 1000 mm"
shot cut-1000
check_layout
key ctrl+z
wait 10
shot undone
